
# Sort in Specific Order



## 1. Brute Force Solution

```python
class Solution:
    def sortIt(self, arr):
        n = len(arr)

        for i in range(n):
            for j in range(i + 1, n):
                if (arr[i] % 2 == 0 and arr[j] % 2 == 1) or \
                   (arr[i] % 2 == 1 and arr[j] % 2 == 1 and arr[i] < arr[j]) or \
                   (arr[i] % 2 == 0 and arr[j] % 2 == 0 and arr[i] > arr[j]):
                    arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]

        return arr
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n²)  
**Space Complexity:** O(1)

