## 3. Optimized Solution (Two Pointers + Sorting)

```python
class Solution:
    def sortIt(self, arr):
        n = len(arr)

        left = 0

        # Partition odd and even numbers
        for right in range(n):
            if arr[right] % 2 == 1:
                arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]
                left += 1

        # Sort odd numbers in descending order
        arr[:left] = sorted(arr[:left], reverse=True)

        # Sort even numbers in ascending order
        arr[left:] = sorted(arr[left:])

        return arr
```

**Time Complexity:** O(n log n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(n) due to Python slicing and sorting

